{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794540264953,"sessionID":"ses_e2d114c1cffeCJAo2qUfV4UXZv","part":{"partID":"prt_1d2ef5b71002v4V0cKFuSxqbb0","sessionID":"ses_e2d114c1cffeCJAo2qUfV4UXZv","messageID":"msg_1d2ef5201001H9bywG4yzUUwGa","type":"tool","id":"call_9a16319a37374a1d92704d3a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md, lines 1-239\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one table of tracked commands, attach a typed command to the top recommendation, put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row, measure the typed block in the command capture and add the mirror visibility guard, hook health, a head length test and a brief cost script.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"typed command delivery tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `DB` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `DBC` is `node $DB --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\n33: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `ART` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VART` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `HT` is `$ADV/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` (new) and `VHT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n36: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n37: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (new). `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`. `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\n38: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`. `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` and `VST` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `SRM` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `SRMT` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs` and `SRR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`.\n40: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n43: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a live model session. Running the Claude prompt hook or the advisor CLI is not a model session, and both run in a sandboxed socket directory here.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T024 checks it.\n50: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md`, renames a command or edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: \n53: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n54: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/typed-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n55: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed, because they edit `AR`, `CA`, `ST`, `SCH`, `DSY`, `IG` and `RA`.\n56: - Wave 1: T003 (`DB`, `CA`), T004 (`SRM`, `SRMT`), T005 (`SCH`), T006 (`MBC`), T007 (`IG`).\n57: - Wave 2: T008 (`CA`, `CAT`), T009 (`ST`, `STT`), T010 (`DSY`), T011 (`SRR`).\n58: - Wave 3: T012 (`FU`, `FT`), T013 (`AR`, `ART`), T014 (`HT`).\n59: - Wave 4: T015 (`CAP`), T016 (`AR`).\n60: - Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\n61: - Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\n62: - Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n71: - [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\"-typed-01\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"scorerRow: (true|false) \\},$\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \"'/create:goal': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\},\" $CA` and `rg -n \"'/speckit:resume': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\},\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\n81: - [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n82: - [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\"error\":\"holdout_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\"error\":\"unknown_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\"prompt\":<prompt>,\"cwd\":<root>,\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cost-<id>\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n84: - [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor_recommend --json\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\n85: \n86: ### Wave 2\n87: - [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \"skill.md\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\n91: \n92: ### Wave 3\n93: - [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n95: - [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n96: \n97: ### Wave 4\n98: - [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\"carried\",\"command\",\"expected_command\",\"policy\",\"top\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n99: - [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 5\n102: - [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\n103: - [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\" $RA` prints at least 3.\n104: - [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\n105: \n106: ### Wave 6\n107: - [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n108: - [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n109: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n114: ## Phase 3: Verification\n115: \n116: - [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n117: - [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n118: - [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n119: - [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n125: ## Completion Criteria\n126: \n127: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n128: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n129: - [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\n130: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n135: ## Cross-References\n136: \n137: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n138: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n139: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n140: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## Verification Checklist\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n148: ## Verification Protocol\n149: \n150: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n151: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n152: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n153: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n154: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n155: \n156: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n157: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n162: ## Pre-Implementation\n163: \n164: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the typed row state are in `scratch/` (T001, T002).\n165: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed before wave 1 started.\n166: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n167: \n168: ---\n169: \n170: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n171: ## Code Quality\n172: \n173: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n174: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T024).\n175: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The generated block is written by the deriver only, and its check prints `fresh` (T003, T022).\n176: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A prompt with no typed command leaves the recommendation unchanged (T012, T013).\n177: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n178: \n179: ---\n180: \n181: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n182: ## Testing Checklist\n183: \n184: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T022).\n185: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The baseline reads 44 of 44 typed and the slice test passes (T017).\n186: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The parity test and the Python test pass (T022).\n187: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The real heads of all 44 typed rows carry their command and a policy (T020).\n188: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n193: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n194: \n195: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `delivery`: the scorer finds the owner, and the command is lost between the scorer and the head.\n196: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the policy table is listed: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|TRACKED_COMMANDS\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n197: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Both return paths of the recommend handler apply the typed step (T013).\n198: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n204: ## Security\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the cost script refuses a holdout row (T006).\n207: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task writes to the home folder or installs anything (T024).\n208: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n213: ## Documentation\n214: \n215: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers.\n216: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the setup asset and the three READMEs match the code (T007, T010, T011, T018, T019).\n217: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n222: ## File Organization\n223: \n224: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, measurements and the hook check live in `scratch/` only.\n225: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n226: \n227: ---\n228: \n229: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n230: ## Verification Summary\n231: \n232: | Category | Total | Verified |\n233: |----------|-------|----------|\n234: | P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n235: | P1 Items | 7 | 0/7 |\n236: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n237: \n238: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md, lines 1-239\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\"\n3: description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that generate one table of tracked commands, attach a typed command to the top recommendation, put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row, measure the typed block in the command capture and add the mirror visibility guard, hook health, a head length test and a brief cost script.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"typed command delivery tasks\"\n6: importance_tier: \"normal\"\n7: contextType: \"general\"\n8: ---\n9: <!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.4 -->\n10: # Tasks: Phase 11: typed-command-delivery-and-guards\n11: \n12: <!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n13: \n14: ---\n15: \n16: <!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n17: ## Task Notation\n18: \n19: | Prefix | Meaning |\n20: |--------|---------|\n21: | `[ ]` | Pending |\n22: | `[x]` | Completed |\n23: | `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n24: | `[B]` | Blocked |\n25: | `[C]` | Coordinator task: a live model session, an arena or an operator step. No worker runs it |\n26: \n27: **Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n28: \n29: Every command runs from the repository root unless a task says otherwise.\n30: - `ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`. `TC` is `npm run typecheck` in `ADV`, which must exit 0. `BLD` is `npm run build` in `ADV`, which must exit 0.\n31: - `CA` is `$ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` and `CAT` its test `$ADV/tests/command-attach.vitest.ts`. `VCA` is `npx vitest run tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n32: - `DB` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`. `DBC` is `node $DB --check | jq -r .status`, which must print `fresh`. `CBR` is `$ADV/scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\n33: - `FU` is `$ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`. `FT` is `$ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` (new) and `VFT` is `npx vitest run tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n34: - `AR` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`. `ART` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` (new) and `VART` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-typed-command.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n35: - `HT` is `$ADV/tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` (new) and `VHT` is `npx vitest run tests/command-head-length.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n36: - `CAP` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`. `BASE` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-routing-baseline.json`. `CORPUS` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl`. `RS` is `npx vitest run tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` in `ADV`. `RA` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md`.\n37: - `MBC` is `$ADV/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (new). `OF` is `$ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`. `HOOK` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/dist/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js`.\n38: - `SCH` is `$ADV/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`. `ST` is `$ADV/handlers/advisor-status.ts`. `STT` is `$ADV/tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts` and `VST` is `npx vitest run tests/handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV`.\n39: - `SRM` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `SRMT` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/sync-runtime-mirrors.test.mjs` and `SRR` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/README.md`.\n40: - `DS` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts`. `DSY` is `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`. `DCT` is `node --test $DS/tests/doctor-runtime-mirrors-contract.test.cjs $DS/tests/doctor-setup-orphan-line.test.cjs`. `IG` is `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`. `SP` is this phase's `scratch/` folder.\n41: - `FLOOR` is `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer'`, which must print at least `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and exactly `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n42: - `EVAL` is `node $ADV/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs | jq -c '[.metrics.full_corpus_top1.correct,.metrics.holdout_top1.correct,.metrics.ambiguity_top1.correct,.metrics.gold_none_false_fire.value]'`, which must print numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5.\n43: - `PY` is `python3 $ADV/tests/python/test_skill_advisor.py`, which must exit 0. `PAR` is `npx vitest run tests/parity/python-ts-parity.vitest.ts` in `ADV`, which must report 0 failed.\n44: \n45: Rules for every task:\n46: - Each task is one change to the files it names. A task that names a module and its test adds the behaviour and the cases that pin it.\n47: - No task reads or prints holdout prompt text. A script filters on `split` before it uses a prompt and prints row ids only.\n48: - No worker starts a live model session. Running the Claude prompt hook or the advisor CLI is not a model session, and both run in a sandboxed socket directory here.\n49: - No code comment may name a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id. State the durable reason instead. T024 checks it.\n50: - No task writes to the home folder, installs anything, edits `AGENTS.md`, renames a command or edits a file under `.skilled/commands/create/`.\n51: - A `.md` edit routes through `sk-doc` and a code edit through `sk-code` before the first write.\n52: \n53: Worker waves. Tasks in one wave touch different files and can run in parallel. Each task owns the files in parentheses.\n54: - Wave 0: T001 (`$SP/before.txt`), T002 (`$SP/typed-before.json`). Read-only for the repository.\n55: - Gate: no task from wave 1 on starts before the coordinator confirms that phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed, because they edit `AR`, `CA`, `ST`, `SCH`, `DSY`, `IG` and `RA`.\n56: - Wave 1: T003 (`DB`, `CA`), T004 (`SRM`, `SRMT`), T005 (`SCH`), T006 (`MBC`), T007 (`IG`).\n57: - Wave 2: T008 (`CA`, `CAT`), T009 (`ST`, `STT`), T010 (`DSY`), T011 (`SRR`).\n58: - Wave 3: T012 (`FU`, `FT`), T013 (`AR`, `ART`), T014 (`HT`).\n59: - Wave 4: T015 (`CAP`), T016 (`AR`).\n60: - Wave 5: T017 (`BASE`), T018 (`RA`), T019 (`CBR`).\n61: - Wave 6, one at a time because both start a sandboxed daemon: T020 (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`), T021 (`$SP/brief-cost.json`).\n62: - Verification, one at a time: T022, T023, T024, T025.\n63: <!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n64: \n65: ---\n66: \n67: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n68: ## Phase 1: Setup\n69: \n70: - [x] T001 Record the before numbers (`$SP/before.txt`). Run `FLOOR`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3, .metrics.typed_reach_top3, .metrics.agreement, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached, .attachedMetrics.plain'`, `EVAL`, `TC`, `PY`, `DBC`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VST`, `node --test $SRMT`, `node $SRM --check` and `DCT`, and write each command with its last output line or exit code into `before.txt`. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than `[159,50,20]` and a fourth no higher than 5, `TC` and `PY` exit 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `node $SRM --check` exits 0 and `wc -l < $SP/before.txt` prints at least 15. When a gate is red here, stop and mark the phase `[B]` with that line, because a red before number cannot be held.\n71: - [x] T002 Record each typed row's state (`$SP/typed-before.json`): run `node $CAP | jq '[.rows | to_entries[] | select(.key | endswith(\"-typed-01\")) | {id: .key, top: .value.top, top1: .value.top1}] as $t | .attachedMetrics.attachedRows as $a | [$t[] | . + {attached: ($a[.id] // null)}]' > $SP/typed-before.json`. Verify: `jq 'length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 44, `jq '[.[] | select(.top1)] | length' $SP/typed-before.json` prints 24 and `jq -r '.[] | keys[]' $SP/typed-before.json | sort -u | tr '\\n' ' '` prints `attached id top top1 `.\n72: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n77: ## Phase 2: Implementation\n78: \n79: ### Wave 1\n80: - [ ] T003 [P] Generate one table of every tracked command (`DB`, `CA`). In `CA`, above `// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND ROWS`, add `export interface TrackedCommand { readonly policy: 'run' | 'start' | 'ask'; readonly ownerSkillId: string; readonly scorerRow: boolean; }` with a comment saying the table covers every tracked command, whether or not its bridge is active, so a typed command always has a policy and an owner. In `DB`'s `renderCommandRows(entries, policies)`, build a third map over every entry, with no enabled filter: key `entryRunnable(entry)`, value `{ policy: runnablePolicy(runnable, policies), ownerSkillId: entry.skillId, scorerRow: entry.runtime.typescript.enabled === true }`. Throw `[command-bridges] Conflicting tracked command <runnable>` when one runnable repeats with a different owner or policy. Render it after the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block as `export const TRACKED_COMMANDS: Readonly<Record<string, TrackedCommand>> = {` with one line per key in sorted order, shaped `  '<runnable>': { policy: '<policy>', ownerSkillId: '<owner>', scorerRow: <true|false> },`, and `};`. Run `node $DB`. Do not edit the generated block by hand. Verify: `DBC` prints `fresh`, `rg -c \"scorerRow: (true|false) \\},$\" $CA` prints at least 44, `rg -n \"'/create:goal': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'sk-doc', scorerRow: false \\},\" $CA` and `rg -n \"'/speckit:resume': \\{ policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit', scorerRow: true \\},\" $CA` each print one line, `TC` exits 0, `npx vitest run tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --stat HEAD -- $ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py $ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts` prints nothing.\n81: - [ ] T004 [P] Add a command visibility count and a collapse guard to the mirror check (`SRM`, `SRMT`). Add `const COLLAPSE_ALLOWLIST = new Set(['create/skill.md'])` with a comment saying Claude Code reads a command folder holding `skill.md` as one skill and hides its siblings, and the existing case is kept until the commands are renamed. Add and export `commandVisibility(expectedLinks)`: it takes the `claude-commands` links whose path below `.claude/commands/` holds a folder, counts them as `total`, and counts Claude's `visible` as one per folder that holds `skill.md` plus every command in the other folders. Cursor's `visible` is `total`, because Cursor uses flat names. Add and export `collapseDrift(expectedLinks)`, which returns `COLLAPSE <folder>/skill.md hides <n> sibling commands on Claude Code` for each folder holding `skill.md` whose path is not in the allowlist. In `checkMirrors`, add those lines to `drift`, and before the PASS line print `[runtime-mirror-sync] visibility claude <visible>/<total>, cursor <total>/<total>`. Keep the PASS line as it is. In `SRMT`, add one case where synthetic links for `create/skill.md`, `create/readme.md` and `deep/review.md` give `{ claude: { visible: 2, total: 3 }, cursor: { visible: 3, total: 3 } }` and no drift, and one where an added `design/skill.md` beside `design/chart.md` gives `['COLLAPSE design/skill.md hides 1 sibling commands on Claude Code']`. Verify: `node --test $SRMT` reports `fail 0`, `node $SRM --check` prints a line containing `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` and exits 0, and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n82: - [ ] T005 [P] Add `hookHealth` to the status output schema (`SCH`). In `AdvisorStatusOutputSchema`, after `embeddingsHealth`, add `hookHealth: z.object({ invocations: z.number().int().positive(), rollingP95Ms: z.number().nonnegative(), rollingFailOpenRate: z.number().min(0).max(1), rollingCacheHitRate: z.number().min(0).max(1) }).strict().optional()`. Verify: `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $SCH` prints 1 and `npx vitest run tests/schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.vitest.ts` in `ADV` reports 0 failed.\n83: - [ ] T006 [P] Create `MBC`. `node $MBC [--rows <id,id>] [--root <dir>]` reads `CORPUS` under `--root` (default the current directory), keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, and with `--rows` keeps only the named ids, exiting 2 with `{\"error\":\"holdout_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for a row whose split is `holdout` and `{\"error\":\"unknown_row\",\"id\":\"<id>\"}` for an id it cannot find, before it spawns anything. It makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-cost-'))`, and for each row pipes `{\"prompt\":<prompt>,\"cwd\":<root>,\"hook_event_name\":\"UserPromptSubmit\",\"session_id\":\"cost-<id>\"}` into `node <root>/$HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to that directory and a 30,000 ms timeout. It takes `hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext` (or the empty string), and records `bytes` as its UTF-8 length and `estimatedTokens` as `Math.ceil(bytes / 4)`, the renderer's own four characters per token. It prints one JSON object `{ rows: [{ id, bytes, estimatedTokens }], totalBytes, medianBytes, maxBytes }` and never prints a prompt. At the end it sends `SIGTERM` only to a process whose command line names that directory and removes the directory. Verify: `node --check $MBC` exits 0, `node $MBC --rows cmd-speckit-save-typed-01 | jq -c '.rows[0] | [.id, (.bytes > 0), (.estimatedTokens == ((.bytes + 3) / 4 | floor))]'` prints `[\"cmd-speckit-save-typed-01\",true,true]`, `node $MBC --rows \"$(jq -r 'select(.split==\"holdout\") | .id' $CORPUS | head -1)\"` exits 2 and prints `holdout_row`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n84: - [ ] T007 [P] In `IG`, under `### Check the Install`, add one paragraph after the paragraph about Codex hook approval: to see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`. Re-read the section first, because phase 008 also edits section 2. Verify: `rg -c \"advisor_recommend --json\" $IG` prints 1, and the documented command prints one line that is neither empty nor `null`.\n85: \n86: ### Wave 2\n87: - [ ] T008 [P] Add two typed command helpers (`CA`, `CAT`). `typedCommandIn(prompt)` lowercases the prompt and returns the longest `TRACKED_COMMANDS` key found at a position where the character before it is absent, whitespace, a backtick, a quote or `(`, and the character after it is absent or not a word character, colon or hyphen. It returns undefined when none is found. `typedCommandForTop(topSkillId, prompt)` takes that key and returns `{ command, policy, ownerSkillId }` from its row when `topSkillId` is the row's `ownerSkillId` or `commandRowFor(topSkillId)?.command` equals the key, and undefined otherwise. In `CAT`, add cases: `/create:skill-parent deploy-hub with three modes` gives `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:sk` gives undefined, `see docs/create:goal.md` gives undefined, `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives `{ command: '/speckit:resume', policy: 'start', ownerSkillId: 'system-spec-kit' }`, `typedCommandForTop('command-speckit-resume', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives the same and `typedCommandForTop('sk-doc', '/speckit:resume cache work')` gives undefined. Verify: `VCA` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n88: - [ ] T009 [P] Report hook health in the status (`ST`, `STT`). Run after phase 008, which edits `readSemanticLaneHealth` and `handleAdvisorStatus` in the same file. In `readAdvisorStatus`, in the `output` object of the success path (the one inside `try`, right after `laneWeights: DEFAULT_SCORER_WEIGHTS,`), add `hookHealth` from `readAdvisorHookHealthSection(workspaceRoot)` (`$ADV/lib/metrics.ts`) when its `lastInvocations` is not empty: `invocations` is the length of `lastInvocations` and the three rolling fields copy over. Leave the error path as it is. Add a comment saying the p95 counts cache-hit invocations only. In `STT`, add one case that writes two valid diagnostic records with `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` for a temporary workspace root and reads `hookHealth.invocations` 2, and one case for a root with no records that reads no `hookHealth` key. Verify: `VST` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n89: - [ ] T010 [P] Show hook health under the setup advisor leg (`DSY`). Run after phase 008, which adds an embedder leg after this one. In the single list item that starts `- \"Leg advisor:`, append before its closing quote: ` When data.hookHealth is present, show hook p95 <rollingP95Ms> ms over <invocations> prompts and fail-open <rollingFailOpenRate as a percent> under the leg. It never changes the leg's status.` Change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c \"hookHealth\" $DSY` prints 1 and `DCT` reports `fail 0`.\n90: - [ ] T011 [P] In `SRR` section 5, add two sentences after the check command: the check also prints how many tracked commands each runtime shows, and it fails when a command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`, because Claude Code would then hide that folder's other commands. Verify: `rg -n \"skill.md\" $SRR` prints at least one line in section 5.\n91: \n92: ### Wave 3\n93: - [ ] T012 [P] Put the owner first for a typed command with no scorer row (`FU`, `FT`). Import `typedCommandIn` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from `../command-attach.js`. Export `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower)`: when `typedCommandIn(promptLower)` names a row with `scorerRow` false and that row's owner is at an index above 0 with `passes_threshold` true, return the list with the owner moved to index 0 and every other entry in its order. Otherwise return `ranked` unchanged. In `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, call `ranked = rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst(ranked, promptLower);` right after the `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` statement and before `const passing`. Add a comment saying a typed command with no row of its own can only reach the reader through its owner, so the owner must lead. In `FT`, add cases on synthetic lists: `/create:goal x` with `sk-doc` passing at index 1 moves it first, the same with `sk-doc` not passing changes nothing, `/speckit:save x` (a command with a scorer row) changes nothing and a prompt with no slash changes nothing. Verify: `VFT` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n94: - [ ] T013 [P] Attach a typed command to the top recommendation (`AR`, `ART`). Import `typedCommandForTop` from `../lib/command-attach.js` and export `attachTypedCommand(output, prompt)`: when `output.recommendations[0]` exists and `typedCommandForTop(top.skillId, prompt)` returns a row, return `AdvisorRecommendOutputSchema.parse` of the output with the first recommendation's `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` set from that row, replacing any compiled route command. Otherwise return `output` itself. In `computeRecommendationOutput`, wrap both final returns, the cached one and the last one, as `return attachTypedCommand(<the existing expression>, input.prompt);`. Add a comment saying a typed command is the reader's own choice, so it outranks a routed mode. In `ART`, add cases: a top `system-spec-kit` with prompt `/speckit:resume cache work` carries `/speckit:resume`, `start` and `system-spec-kit`, a top `sk-doc` already carrying `/create:readme` with prompt `/create:goal retrofit` carries `/create:goal` and `start`, a top `mcp-tooling` with that prompt returns the same object and a prompt with no slash returns the same object. Verify: `VART` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0.\n95: - [ ] T014 [P] Create `HT`. For every key of `TRACKED_COMMANDS`, render `renderAdvisorBrief` with one passing `skill` recommendation for the row's owner that carries the key as `command`, its `policy` and its `ownerSkillId`, freshness `live` and `metrics: { tokenCap: 80 }`, in the shape `$ADV/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` uses. Do the same for every id in `COMMAND_ROWS` as a `command` recommendation. Take the head before `DIRECTIVES_LABEL` and assert that `Buffer.byteLength(head, 'utf8')` is at most `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT`, that the head does not end with `...` and that it contains `<command> (<policy>)`. Define `HEAD_BYTE_LIMIT` as `80 * 4` with a comment naming the renderer's default token cap and its four characters per token. Add one case where a synthetic 330-character command fails the same check. Verify: `VHT` reports 0 failed and at least 45 passed tests.\n96: \n97: ### Wave 4\n98: - [ ] T015 Add the typed block to the command capture (`CAP`). Import `typedCommandForTop` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` from the built attach module the script already loads. For each row with `row_type` `typed`, compute `delivered` as `typedCommandForTop(topId, row.prompt)?.command ?? attached`, the same precedence as the handler, and `policy` as `TRACKED_COMMANDS[delivered]?.policy ?? null`. Count `own` when `top1Hit`, else `attached` when `delivered` equals the expected command and `policy` is not null, in a tally built with `emptyAttachedTally` and `addAttachedRow`. Add `typed: attachedTallyJson(...)` to `attachedMetrics`, and `typedRows`, keyed by row id in sorted order, each `{ expected_command, top, carried, command, policy }`, where `carried` is `own`, `attached` or null. Write no prompt text. Leave every existing key and its computation unchanged. Verify: after `BLD`, `node $CAP | jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed'` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `node $CAP | jq -c '[.attachedMetrics.typedRows[] | keys] | unique'` prints `[[\"carried\",\"command\",\"expected_command\",\"policy\",\"top\"]]` and `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`.\n99: - [ ] T016 Take a hub-attached command's policy from the new table (`AR`). In `enrichCompiledRoutes`, replace the spread that reads `COMMAND_POLICIES` with `...(Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command) ? { policy: TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy } : {})`, import `TRACKED_COMMANDS` and drop `COMMAND_POLICIES` from the import when nothing else uses it. Verify: `rg -c \"COMMAND_POLICIES\" $AR` prints nothing or 0, `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS\\[command\\]\" $AR` prints 1, `TC` exits 0 and `VART` reports 0 failed.\n100: \n101: ### Wave 5\n102: - [ ] T017 Rebuild and recapture the command baseline (`BASE`). Run `BLD`, then `node $CAP --write`. Verify: `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.typed' $BASE` prints `{\"own\":24,\"attached\":20,\"combined\":44,\"total\":44}`, `jq -c '.metrics.typed_recall_at_1, .metrics.false_offer, .attachedMetrics.false_offer_attached' $BASE` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}`, `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `jq '.metrics.slash_variant.reached_top3' $BASE` prints at least the value in `$SP/before.txt`, `jq -c '.attachedMetrics.plain' $BASE` equals the line in `$SP/before.txt` and `RS` reports 0 failed.\n103: - [ ] T018 [P] In `RA`, describe `attachedMetrics.typed` and `attachedMetrics.typedRows`, the rule that a typed command travels on its owner, and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` with its flags, its output keys and its sandbox. Verify: `rg -c \"attachedMetrics.typed|typedRows|measure-brief-cost\" $RA` prints at least 3.\n104: - [ ] T019 [P] In `CBR`, describe `TRACKED_COMMANDS`: one row per bridge entry with its policy, its owner and `scorerRow`, generated whether or not the bridge is active. Verify: `rg -c \"TRACKED_COMMANDS|scorerRow\" $CBR` prints at least 2.\n105: \n106: ### Wave 6\n107: - [ ] T020 Check the real heads (`$SP/typed-heads.mjs`, `$SP/typed-heads.json`). Write a script that reads `CORPUS`, keeps rows with `row_type` `typed` and `split` `none`, makes one directory with `mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'ssa-typed-'))`, pipes each row's payload (the shape of T006, session id `typed-<id>`) into `node $HOOK` with `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR` set to it, takes the first line of `additionalContext` and reads it with `parseOffer` from `OF`. It writes `[{ id, offeredCommand, offeredPolicy, commandMatches, policyPresent, labelAgrees }]` to `typed-heads.json`, where `commandMatches` compares the `/<namespace>:<name>` part of the offer with the row's `expected_command`, `policyPresent` is true for `run`, `start` or `ask` and `labelAgrees` compares the policy with the row's `expected_policy`. It stops and removes its sandbox as T006 does and prints no prompt. Verify: `jq '[.[] | select(.commandMatches and .policyPresent)] | length' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints 44, `jq -r '[.[] | select(.labelAgrees | not) | .id] | join(\",\")' $SP/typed-heads.json` prints `cmd-design-extract-typed-01,cmd-doctor-env-typed-01,cmd-doctor-update-typed-01` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-typed-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n108: - [ ] T021 Measure the brief cost (`$SP/brief-cost.json`). Run `node $MBC > $SP/brief-cost.json`. Verify: `jq '.rows | length' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints 44, `jq '.maxBytes > 0 and .medianBytes > 0' $SP/brief-cost.json` prints `true` and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-cost-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n109: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: <!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n114: ## Phase 3: Verification\n115: \n116: - [ ] T022 Run every floor. Verify: `FLOOR` prints `{\"correct\":24,\"total\":44}` and `{\"count\":0,\"total\":35}`, `EVAL` prints numbers no lower than its line in `$SP/before.txt` and no lower than `[159,50,20]` with the fourth no higher than 5, `TC` exits 0, `PY` exits 0, `DBC` prints `fresh`, `RS`, `PAR`, `VCA`, `VFT`, `VART`, `VHT` and `VST` report 0 failed, `node --test $SRMT` and `DCT` report `fail 0` and `node $SRM --check` exits 0. Write the outputs beside the before lines in `$SP/after.txt`.\n117: - [ ] T023 Read hook health live. Make one directory with `D=$(mktemp -d \"$TMPDIR/ssa-status-XXXXXX\")`, run `SPECKIT_IPC_SOCKET_DIR=\"$D\" node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \"$PWD\" --format json --no-warm-only | jq -r '.data.hookHealth.rollingP95Ms | type'`, then stop only a process whose command line names `$D` and remove `$D`. The Claude prompt hook runs in T020 and T021 wrote the diagnostic records it reads. Verify: the command prints `number`, and `ls -d \"$TMPDIR\"/ssa-status-* 2>/dev/null` prints nothing.\n118: - [ ] T024 Check the boundaries. Verify: `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff --quiet HEAD -- AGENTS.md .skilled/commands/create` exits 0, `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff HEAD -U0 -- .skilled | rg \"^\\+.*(//|#|\\*).*(specs/|REQ-0|ADR-0|T0[0-9]{2}|phase [0-9])\"` prints nothing and `git -c core.fsmonitor=false status --short -- .skilled INSTALL-SKILLED.md AGENTS.md` lists only files named in this phase's tasks.\n119: - [ ] T025 Write `implementation-summary.md` and mark each row in `acceptance-criteria.md` with its evidence. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh <this folder> --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n120: <!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n121: \n122: ---\n123: \n124: <!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n125: ## Completion Criteria\n126: \n127: - [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n128: - [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n129: - [ ] The committed baseline reads `attachedMetrics.typed.combined` 44 of 44 and every floor holds against `scratch/before.txt`\n130: <!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: <!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n135: ## Cross-References\n136: \n137: - **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n138: - **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n139: - **Acceptance criteria**: See `acceptance-criteria.md`\n140: - **Research**: `../009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md`\n141: <!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## Verification Checklist\n146: \n147: <!-- ANCHOR:protocol -->\n148: ## Verification Protocol\n149: \n150: | Priority | Handling | Completion Impact |\n151: |----------|----------|-------------------|\n152: | **[P0]** | HARD BLOCKER | Cannot claim done until complete |\n153: | **[P1]** | Required | Must complete OR get user approval |\n154: | **[P2]** | Optional | Can defer with documented reason |\n155: \n156: A blocked task gets `[B]` and one line naming what blocks it. A moved floor blocks the phase.\n157: <!-- /ANCHOR:protocol -->\n158: \n159: ---\n160: \n161: <!-- ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n162: ## Pre-Implementation\n163: \n164: - [ ] CHK-001 [P0] The before numbers and the typed row state are in `scratch/` (T001, T002).\n165: - [ ] CHK-002 [P0] The coordinator confirmed phases 005, 008 and 010 are committed before wave 1 started.\n166: <!-- /ANCHOR:pre-impl -->\n167: \n168: ---\n169: \n170: <!-- ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n171: ## Code Quality\n172: \n173: - [ ] CHK-010 [P0] `npm run typecheck` in `ADV` exits 0.\n174: - [ ] CHK-011 [P0] No code comment names a spec path, a phase number, a task id, an ADR or a REQ id (T024).\n175: - [ ] CHK-012 [P0] The generated block is written by the deriver only, and its check prints `fresh` (T003, T022).\n176: - [ ] CHK-013 [P1] A prompt with no typed command leaves the recommendation unchanged (T012, T013).\n177: <!-- /ANCHOR:code-quality -->\n178: \n179: ---\n180: \n181: <!-- ANCHOR:testing -->\n182: ## Testing Checklist\n183: \n184: - [ ] CHK-020 [P0] Every floor holds (T022).\n185: - [ ] CHK-021 [P0] The baseline reads 44 of 44 typed and the slice test passes (T017).\n186: - [ ] CHK-022 [P0] The parity test and the Python test pass (T022).\n187: - [ ] CHK-023 [P1] The real heads of all 44 typed rows carry their command and a policy (T020).\n188: <!-- /ANCHOR:testing -->\n189: \n190: ---\n191: \n192: <!-- ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n193: ## FIX ADDENDUM: FIX COMPLETENESS\n194: \n195: - [ ] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] The gap is class `delivery`: the scorer finds the owner, and the command is lost between the scorer and the head.\n196: - [ ] CHK-FIX-002 [P0] Every reader of the policy table is listed: `rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|TRACKED_COMMANDS\" .skilled --glob '!**/node_modules/**' --glob '!**/dist/**'`.\n197: - [ ] CHK-FIX-003 [P1] Both return paths of the recommend handler apply the typed step (T013).\n198: - [ ] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] Evidence names the commit it ran on.\n199: <!-- /ANCHOR:fix-completeness -->\n200: \n201: ---\n202: \n203: <!-- ANCHOR:security -->\n204: ## Security\n205: \n206: - [ ] CHK-030 [P0] No task reads or prints holdout prompt text, and the cost script refuses a holdout row (T006).\n207: - [ ] CHK-031 [P0] No task writes to the home folder or installs anything (T024).\n208: <!-- /ANCHOR:security -->\n209: \n210: ---\n211: \n212: <!-- ANCHOR:docs -->\n213: ## Documentation\n214: \n215: - [ ] CHK-040 [P1] `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md` and `implementation-summary.md` state the same numbers.\n216: - [ ] CHK-041 [P1] The install guide, the setup asset and the three READMEs match the code (T007, T010, T011, T018, T019).\n217: <!-- /ANCHOR:docs -->\n218: \n219: ---\n220: \n221: <!-- ANCHOR:file-org -->\n222: ## File Organization\n223: \n224: - [ ] CHK-050 [P1] Probes, measurements and the hook check live in `scratch/` only.\n225: <!-- /ANCHOR:file-org -->\n226: \n227: ---\n228: \n229: <!-- ANCHOR:summary -->\n230: ## Verification Summary\n231: \n232: | Category | Total | Verified |\n233: |----------|-------|----------|\n234: | P0 Items | 12 | 0/12 |\n235: | P1 Items | 7 | 0/7 |\n236: | P2 Items | 0 | 0/0 |\n237: \n238: **Verification Date**: 2026-11-13\n239: <!-- /ANCHOR:summary -->"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/tasks.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794540264305,"end":1794540264953}}}}
